msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Use AI skills (optional)\">\n"
"To deploy your own code with help from an AI assistant, use the AI skills in the [Qiskit Function templates repository](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Use habilidades de IA (opcional)\">\n"
"Para implantar seu próprio código com a ajuda de um assistente de IA, use as habilidades de IA do [repositório de modelos de Qiskit Function](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write a workflow {#write-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Escreva um workflow {#write-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the folder structure {#create-the-folder-structure}"
msgstr "Crie a estrutura de pastas {#create-the-folder-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow is a folder of Python files with one entrypoint file. A managed workflow uploads everything in the folder, up to 50 MB, and runs the entrypoint as a script. Because a workflow uploads the whole folder, keep your local files, such as `deploy.ipynb`, outside the folder. Create the following layout:\n"
msgstr "Um workflow gerenciado é uma pasta de arquivos Python com um arquivo de ponto de entrada. Um workflow gerenciado envia tudo o que está na pasta, até 50 MB, e executa o ponto de entrada como um script. Como o workflow envia a pasta inteira, mantenha seus arquivos locais, como `deploy.ipynb`, fora da pasta. Crie o seguinte layout:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the hello world entrypoint {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"
msgstr "Escreva o ponto de entrada hello world {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint reads a circuit, optimizes and simulates it, and saves the counts and two-qubit depth. Save the following code as `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"
msgstr "O ponto de entrada lê um circuito, o otimiza e o simula, e salva as contagens e a profundidade de dois qubits. Salve o código a seguir como `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you read this page as a notebook, the code cell for `hello_world.py` starts with the `%%writefile` [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile). When you run this cell, it saves the code to the file instead of running the code.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Se você ler esta página como um notebook, a célula de código de `hello_world.py` começa com o [comando mágico](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile) `%%writefile`. Ao executar essa célula, ela salva o código no arquivo em vez de executá-lo.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint uses three functions from `qiskit_serverless`:\n"
msgstr "O ponto de entrada usa três funções de `qiskit_serverless`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_arguments()` returns the keyword arguments that you pass to `run()`, as a dictionary. Each value must be JSON-serializable, or an object that the client can encode, such as a `QuantumCircuit`. Encoded objects arrive as the same objects that you passed.\n"
msgstr "`get_arguments()` retorna, como um dicionário, os argumentos nomeados que você passa para `run()`. Cada valor deve ser serializável em JSON ou um objeto que o cliente consiga codificar, como um `QuantumCircuit`. Os objetos codificados chegam como os mesmos objetos que você passou.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` sets the detailed status `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, which you can see while the job runs. See [Report progress with update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"
msgstr "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` define o status detalhado `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, que você pode ver enquanto o job é executado. Consulte [Informar o progresso com update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`save_result()` stores a JSON-serializable value that you read later with `job.result()`. The workflow returns the counts as a dictionary and the two-qubit depth of the optimized circuit as an integer.\n"
msgstr "`save_result()` armazena um valor serializável em JSON que você lê depois com `job.result()`. O workflow retorna as contagens como um dicionário e a profundidade de dois qubits do circuito otimizado como um inteiro.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output, such as the two-qubit depth, goes to the job's logs. To add timestamps and log levels, use the `logging` module. See [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"
msgstr "Tudo o que o workflow escreve na saída padrão, como a profundidade de dois qubits, vai para os logs do job. Para adicionar carimbos de data e hora e níveis de log, use o módulo `logging`. Consulte [Escrever logs e tratar erros](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Envie o workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In your local notebook, run the following code from the `hello_world_project` folder. The code connects with your saved account, defines the workflow, and uploads it. `entrypoint` is the file that the workflow runs, and `working_dir` is the folder that you upload:\n"
msgstr "No seu notebook local, execute o código a seguir a partir da pasta `hello_world_project`. O código se conecta com sua conta salva, define o workflow e o envia. `entrypoint` é o arquivo que o workflow executa, e `working_dir` é a pasta que você envia:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the workflow with inputs {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"
msgstr "Execute o workflow com entradas {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct a three-qubit GHZ circuit to pass to `hello_world` as an input:\n"
msgstr "Construa um circuito GHZ de três qubits para passar a `hello_world` como entrada:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run `hello_world` with the circuit and the number of shots as keyword arguments. The argument names match the keys that the entrypoint reads with `get_arguments()`:\n"
msgstr "Execute `hello_world` com o circuito e o número de shots como argumentos nomeados. Os nomes dos argumentos correspondem às chaves que o ponto de entrada lê com `get_arguments()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`run()` returns a `Job` after the workflow queues the job. It does not wait for the job to run. The job continues in the cloud after you close your Python session. To find it again later, list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "`run()` retorna um `Job` depois que o workflow coloca o job na fila. Ele não espera o job ser executado. O job continua na nuvem depois que você fecha sua sessão Python. Para encontrá-lo novamente mais tarde, liste seus jobs recentes com `client.jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: add the web UI for job history when it is available. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the status, result, and logs {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"
msgstr "Obtenha o status, o resultado e os logs {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
msgstr "Imediatamente depois de chamar `run()`, o status geralmente é `QUEUED`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The status changes from `QUEUED` to `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING`, and then `DONE`.\n"
msgstr "O status muda de `QUEUED` para `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING` e, em seguida, `DONE`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to `save_result()`:\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` espera até o job terminar e então retorna o valor que o workflow passou para `save_result()`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can read the logs while the job runs. The workflow uploads new lines about every 15 seconds. The logs include the line that the workflow printed:\n"
msgstr "Você pode ler os logs enquanto o job é executado. O workflow envia novas linhas aproximadamente a cada 15 segundos. Os logs incluem a linha que o workflow imprimiu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the workflow {#update-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Atualize o workflow {#update-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To change a workflow, edit its files and call `upload()` again with the same `title`. The new upload replaces the earlier one, and jobs that already started are not affected.\n"
msgstr "Para alterar um workflow, edite seus arquivos e chame `upload()` novamente com o mesmo `title`. O novo envio substitui o anterior, e os jobs que já começaram não são afetados.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fields such as `arguments_schema` and `sizes_map` keep their stored values when you omit them from the new upload.\n"
msgstr "Campos como `arguments_schema` e `sizes_map` mantêm seus valores armazenados quando você os omite do novo envio.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Próximos passos {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Define inputs and outputs](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) to learn which argument and result types a workflow supports.\n"
"- [Declare dependencies](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) to use more Python packages in your workflow.\n"
"- [Run quantum jobs from a workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) to run your circuits on a QPU, report each stage, and track the QPU jobs.\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to learn all job statuses, debug a failed job, and find a job later.\n"
"- To start from working code, deploy one of the [Qiskit Function templates](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), or adapt a template for your own workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recomendações\">\n"
"- [Defina entradas e saídas](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) para saber quais tipos de argumento e de resultado um workflow suporta.\n"
"- [Declare dependências](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) para usar mais pacotes Python no seu workflow.\n"
"- [Execute jobs quânticos a partir de um workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) para executar seus circuitos em uma QPU, informar cada etapa e acompanhar os jobs da QPU.\n"
"- [Execute um workflow gerenciado](/guides/run-managed-workflow) para conhecer todos os status de job, depurar um job com falha e encontrar um job mais tarde.\n"
"- Para começar a partir de um código funcional, implante um dos [modelos de Qiskit Function](/guides/qiskit-function-templates) ou adapte um modelo para o seu próprio workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
